.TH PAGEFORMER 1 "2026-10-31" "Pageformer 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pageformer \- generate documents from Markdown and a YAML template
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pageformer
.RI [ options ]
.IR input ...
.br
.B pageformer
.B \-\-write\-default\-template
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pageformer
reads each Markdown file or directory and writes one output per input in the
selected format. A directory is walked recursively in path order, and only
.B .md
files are read. Hidden directories and
.B target/
are skipped.
.PP
One template applies to each document: the nearest
.B .pageformer.yaml
above the source, the user template, or the embedded default. The template is
validated for every format, so a broken template fails the same way even when
the format has no equivalent for a style.
.PP
Confidential
.B {NAME}
fields are resolved once, after parsing and before rendering. Their values
come from an INI file or from the user-level folder mapping, and a document
with fields must be written outside its source tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " FILE
Use this template instead of resolving one.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " DIR
Write the generated files under this directory. A directory input mirrors its
relative tree; a direct file is written flat.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Parse the Markdown and validate the template without writing.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " FORMAT
Select
.BR pdf ", " txt ", " odt ", " docx ", " html " or " epub .
The default is
.BR pdf .
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " WHEN
Color the terminal output:
.BR auto ", " always " or " never .
.TP
.BR \-\-confidential\-file " " FILE
Read confidential fields from an INI-style
.B "NAME = value"
file outside the source tree.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-default\-template
Write the embedded template to the user template path and exit. An existing
file is not overwritten. This option takes no input.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .pageformer.yaml
The local template, resolved from the source directory upward.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pageformer/pageformer.yaml
The user template, used when no local template exists. The platform
configuration root replaces
.I ~/.config
where the system defines one. Create it with
.BR pageformer\ \-\-write\-default\-template .
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/pageformer/default.pageformer.yaml
The reference template installed by the Debian package.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when every input succeeds, and one when any input fails. A failure in one
input does not stop the rest of the batch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pageformer-publisher (1)
